{"title": "Soil thin section", "kind": "Method", "weight": "Major", "level": "Advanced", "article": "Thin section", "definition": {"text": "A slice of rock, mineral or soil ground to about 30 μm and mounted on glass for study under a polarizing microscope.", "sent_ids": ["aece27e78a39", "66d6a50bddad", "69d4e7405735"]}, "facts": [{"text": "Soil micromorphology describes far more in thin sections viewed with a petrographic polarizing light microscope than a 10x hand lens can show.", "sent_ids": ["69d4e7405735"]}, {"text": "Between crossed polarizing filters the minerals' optical properties alter the colour and intensity of light, so most rock-forming minerals can be identified.", "sent_ids": ["0828f1eddd9a", "547bc68bc525"]}, {"text": "Thickness is checked with the Michel-Lévy interference colour chart, usually with quartz as the gauge.", "sent_ids": ["0c2f71478525"]}, {"text": "Thin sections reveal the relation of a material's components to one another, features often invisible in a hand specimen.", "sent_ids": ["fed975c626ff", "83bba30681b3"]}, {"text": "Paleosols are identified partly from thin sections: at least 60% recognizable pyroclastic fragments marks an Andisol paleosol.", "sent_ids": ["8418aa2a720b"]}, {"text": "Humus-form horizons have been characterized on thin soil sections by micromorphologists.", "sent_ids": ["d6e5b464a991"]}], "prerequisites": ["soil-form-020", "soil-found-029", "soil-form-134"], "related": ["soil-phys-072", "soil-form-072", "soil-bio-095", "soil-meth-031"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": [], "wants_image": true, "notes": "Thin section and Optical mineralogy pages have no soil sentences; soil facts come from Soil morphology, Paleosol and Humus form. Polarized light microscopy page folded here (PLM sentence 86f6e65c9603 not needed).", "part": "Studying soil: methods and mapping", "chapter": "Soil micromorphology", "id": "soil-meth-030", "score": 15.16, "score_parts": {"importance": 3.584, "weight": 3, "tests": 3, "pages": 2.58, "builds_on_it": 3.0}, "selected": true, "unit": 457, "position": 5, "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "wikipedia", "image": {"file": "File:Esempi di sezioni sottili.jpg", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0", "artist": "Daniele.51", "page_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Esempi_di_sezioni_sottili.jpg", "local": "soil-meth-030.png", "caption": "Daniele.51, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons"}, "curriculum": ["own article", "mentioned on 2+ pages", "prerequisite of 2+"], "sources": [{"title": "Thin section", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thin_section", "revid": 1323745730, "sent_ids": ["0828f1eddd9a", "547bc68bc525", "0c2f71478525", "aece27e78a39", "66d6a50bddad"], "key": "Thin section", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1323745730"}, {"title": "Optical mineralogy", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optical_mineralogy", "revid": 1353527903, "sent_ids": ["fed975c626ff", "83bba30681b3"], "key": "Optical mineralogy", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1353527903"}, {"title": "Humus form", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humus_form", "revid": 1319585501, "sent_ids": ["d6e5b464a991"], "key": "Humus form", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1319585501"}, {"title": "Paleosol", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paleosol", "revid": 1307290060, "sent_ids": ["8418aa2a720b"], "key": "Paleosol", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1307290060"}, {"title": "Soil morphology", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil_morphology", "revid": 1352092346, "sent_ids": ["69d4e7405735"], "key": "Soil morphology", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1352092346"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": "Q542715", "prerequisites_draft": ["soil-form-020"], "prerequisite_sources": {"soil-form-020": "ordering pass", "soil-found-029": "ordering pass", "soil-form-134": "ordering pass"}}
{"title": "Soil biofabric", "kind": "Concept", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Advanced", "article": "Soil biomantle#The biofabric of biomantles", "definition": {"text": "Soil fabric made by organisms, typically small, often pelleted micro- and mesobiofabric left by ants, worms and termites and seen with a hand lens or in soil thin sections.", "sent_ids": ["e81a43755d6f"]}, "facts": [{"text": "As originally defined, a biomantle must show at least 50% biofabric.", "sent_ids": ["0d19deda14ab"]}, {"text": "Burrowing vertebrates and tree uprooting make coarser megabiofabric, cloddy surface spoil heaps for which the 50% criterion is moot.", "sent_ids": ["3742b4ac51b3"]}], "prerequisites": ["soil-meth-030", "soil-form-020", "soil-bio-047", "soil-bio-212", "soil-form-055"], "related": ["soil-bio-047", "soil-meth-030"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": [], "wants_image": false, "notes": null, "part": "Studying soil: methods and mapping", "chapter": "Soil micromorphology", "id": "soil-meth-031", "score": 9.59, "score_parts": {"importance": 6.588, "weight": 0, "tests": 2, "pages": 1.0, "builds_on_it": 0.0}, "selected": true, "unit": 458, "position": 2, "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "wikipedia", "curriculum": ["own section", "hub list"], "sources": [{"title": "Soil biomantle", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil_biomantle", "revid": 1377025715, "sent_ids": ["0d19deda14ab", "3742b4ac51b3", "e81a43755d6f"], "key": "Soil biomantle", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1377025715"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null, "prerequisites_draft": ["soil-form-055", "soil-form-020"], "prerequisite_sources": {"soil-meth-030": "ordering pass", "soil-form-020": "ordering pass", "soil-bio-047": "ordering pass", "soil-bio-212": "ordering pass", "soil-form-055": "consolidation"}}
{"title": "Mineral alteration in thin section", "kind": "Concept", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Advanced", "article": "Optical mineralogy#Alteration Products", "definition": {"text": "The changes natural processes make to a mineral's chemical composition or crystal structure, as they appear under the microscope.", "sent_ids": ["19e60c666ca2"]}, "facts": [{"text": "In thin section some minerals such as feldspar decompose readily and turn turbid, quartz stays fresh and clear, and others yield characteristic secondary products.", "sent_ids": ["ace129d73830"]}, {"text": "Alteration is governed by thermodynamics under the prevailing conditions, with water the most common and influential catalyst.", "sent_ids": ["b0914de4c54d"]}], "prerequisites": ["soil-meth-030", "soil-found-052", "soil-found-029"], "related": ["soil-found-029", "soil-form-020"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": [], "wants_image": false, "notes": "Phrase concept (Mineral weathering in thin section); Optical mineralogy has no soil sentences.", "part": "Studying soil: methods and mapping", "chapter": "Soil micromorphology", "id": "soil-meth-032", "score": 7.47, "score_parts": {"importance": 3.892, "weight": 0, "tests": 2, "pages": 1.58, "builds_on_it": 0.0}, "selected": true, "unit": 458, "position": 4, "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "wikipedia", "curriculum": ["own section", "mentioned on 2+ pages"], "sources": [{"title": "Optical mineralogy", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optical_mineralogy", "revid": 1353527903, "sent_ids": ["ace129d73830"], "key": "Optical mineralogy", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1353527903"}, {"title": "Mineral alteration", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral_alteration", "revid": 1371780307, "sent_ids": ["b0914de4c54d", "19e60c666ca2"], "key": "Mineral alteration", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1371780307"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null, "prerequisites_draft": ["soil-found-052", "soil-meth-030"], "prerequisite_sources": {"soil-meth-030": "ordering pass", "soil-found-052": "ordering pass", "soil-found-029": "ordering pass"}}
{"title": "Soil micromorphology", "kind": "Method", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Intermediate", "article": "Soil morphology#Micromorphology", "definition": {"text": "The description, measurement and interpretation of soil features too small to see with the unaided eye.", "sent_ids": ["9a256dd4097e"]}, "facts": [{"text": "Work may begin in the field with a 10x hand lens, but much more is seen in thin sections under a petrographic polarizing microscope.", "sent_ids": ["69d4e7405735"]}, {"text": "A recognized technique for some 50 years, it spread from pedogenic and paleosol studies to the soils and sediments of archaeological sites.", "sent_ids": ["9c9e238048c0", "ddac2d2774b9"]}, {"text": "Micromorphologists have characterized humus-form horizons on thin soil sections.", "sent_ids": ["d6e5b464a991"]}], "prerequisites": ["soil-form-001"], "related": ["soil-form-072", "soil-found-068", "soil-bio-095"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": ["Soil morphology", "Soil profile", "Horizon designation", "Horizon boundaries"], "wants_image": false, "notes": "The thin-section preparation sentence (S:d24d571c1c4e) carries a citation-needed tag and was not used.", "part": "Studying soil: methods and mapping", "chapter": "Soil micromorphology", "id": "soil-form-020", "score": 23.73, "score_parts": {"importance": 15.147, "weight": 0, "tests": 4, "pages": 1.58, "builds_on_it": 3.0}, "selected": true, "unit": 457, "position": 4, "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "wikipedia", "curriculum": ["own section", "hub list", "mentioned on 2+ pages", "prerequisite of 2+"], "sources": [{"title": "Soil morphology", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil_morphology", "revid": 1352092346, "sent_ids": ["69d4e7405735", "9c9e238048c0", "ddac2d2774b9", "9a256dd4097e"], "key": "Soil morphology", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1352092346"}, {"title": "Humus form", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humus_form", "revid": 1319585501, "sent_ids": ["d6e5b464a991"], "key": "Humus form", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1319585501"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null, "prerequisites_draft": ["soil-form-001"], "prerequisite_sources": {"soil-form-001": "ordering pass"}}
{"title": "Polarized light microscopy", "kind": "Method", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Intermediate", "article": "Polarized light microscopy", "definition": {"text": "Polarized light microscopy covers optical microscopy techniques that illuminate a sample with polarized light, most useful on birefringent samples.", "sent_ids": ["dbfc7b8180e7", "d53e6b7a8109"]}, "facts": [{"text": "A polarizing plate converts natural light into polarized light, and birefringent samples interact strongly with it, giving contrast against the background.", "sent_ids": ["6be4e512ef4c", "d53e6b7a8109"]}, {"text": "It is used extensively in optical mineralogy, the basis of identifying minerals in thin sections.", "sent_ids": ["86f6e65c9603"]}, {"text": "More complex variants include differential interference contrast and interference reflection microscopy.", "sent_ids": ["097b93180a3d"]}], "prerequisites": ["soil-meth-030"], "related": ["soil-form-020"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": [], "wants_image": false, "notes": null, "part": "Studying soil: methods and mapping", "chapter": "Soil micromorphology", "id": "soil-meth-064", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "wikipedia", "curriculum": ["own article"], "sources": [{"title": "Polarized light microscopy", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polarized_light_microscopy", "revid": 1373679842, "sent_ids": ["6be4e512ef4c", "d53e6b7a8109", "86f6e65c9603", "097b93180a3d", "dbfc7b8180e7"], "key": "Polarized light microscopy", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1373679842"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": "Q12046176", "score": 4.77, "score_parts": {"importance": 2.773, "weight": 0, "tests": 1, "pages": 1.0, "builds_on_it": 0.0}, "selected": true, "prerequisites_draft": ["soil-meth-030"], "prerequisite_sources": {"soil-meth-030": "consolidation"}, "unit": 458, "position": 3}
{"title": "X-ray microtomography", "kind": "Method", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Advanced", "article": "X-ray microtomography", "definition": {"text": "X-ray microtomography uses X-rays to make cross-sections of an object at micrometre pixel size and rebuild a 3D model without destroying the sample.", "sent_ids": ["a0ecb47a0556", "9dc46637a5ae"]}, "facts": [{"text": "Also called micro-CT, it is computed tomography in which the sample rotates while source and detector stay still, or the source and detector rotate around the specimen.", "sent_ids": ["9dc46637a5ae", "3fe6d4424f57", "5dd99bfa7ec0"]}, {"text": "Cone-beam systems use a 2D detector to record projection images from which cross-sections are reconstructed.", "sent_ids": ["d7455c5f7063"]}, {"text": "Stacking slices builds a volume of voxels that can be viewed in any plane, and segmentation separates structures that have similar density.", "sent_ids": ["adc771399865", "be5617134516", "29cf5c9582aa", "006c4221bbd7"]}, {"text": "In geology it is used to analyze micropores in reservoir rocks.", "sent_ids": ["096811c46e91"]}], "prerequisites": [], "related": ["soil-phys-070", "soil-phys-072", "soil-phys-171"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": [], "wants_image": false, "notes": "Page has no soil text; included as the non-destructive 3D pore-imaging method named in micromorphology context; soil use rests on the pore/geology sentence only.", "part": "Studying soil: methods and mapping", "chapter": "Soil micromorphology", "id": "soil-meth-065", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "wikipedia", "curriculum": ["own article"], "sources": [{"title": "X-ray microtomography", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X-ray_microtomography", "revid": 1376461558, "sent_ids": ["9dc46637a5ae", "3fe6d4424f57", "5dd99bfa7ec0", "d7455c5f7063", "adc771399865", "be5617134516", "29cf5c9582aa", "006c4221bbd7", "096811c46e91", "a0ecb47a0556"], "key": "X-ray microtomography", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1376461558"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": "Q3042540", "score": 2.0, "score_parts": {"importance": 0.0, "weight": 0, "tests": 1, "pages": 1.0, "builds_on_it": 0.0}, "selected": true, "prerequisites_draft": [], "prerequisite_sources": {}, "unit": 458, "position": 5}
{"title": "Digital image analysis", "kind": "Method", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Intermediate", "article": "Image analysis", "definition": {"text": "Image analysis extracts meaningful information from images, mainly digital ones, by digital image processing.", "sent_ids": ["5dd05a04744a"]}, "facts": [{"text": "Computers are indispensable for large data and quantitative extraction, but human vision still cannot be replaced in many applications.", "sent_ids": ["73a7138c91d1", "d4974f0d4e89"]}, {"text": "Object-based analysis groups pixels into homogeneous objects by segmentation and then classifies them; over-segmentation is often preferred when classifying high-resolution images.", "sent_ids": ["f2169bb355e2", "5b310a0148cc", "6e3a588d83cf"]}, {"text": "It is applied in metallography, for instance to determine the mineral content of a rock sample.", "sent_ids": ["28097d733a6c"]}], "prerequisites": [], "related": ["soil-phys-072", "soil-meth-030"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": [], "wants_image": false, "notes": null, "part": "Studying soil: methods and mapping", "chapter": "Soil micromorphology", "id": "soil-meth-066", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "wikipedia", "curriculum": ["own article"], "sources": [{"title": "Image analysis", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image_analysis", "revid": 1366780900, "sent_ids": ["73a7138c91d1", "d4974f0d4e89", "f2169bb355e2", "5b310a0148cc", "6e3a588d83cf", "28097d733a6c", "5dd05a04744a"], "key": "Image analysis", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1366780900"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": "Q860755", "score": 5.58, "score_parts": {"importance": 3.584, "weight": 0, "tests": 1, "pages": 1.0, "builds_on_it": 0.0}, "selected": true, "prerequisites_draft": [], "prerequisite_sources": {}, "unit": 458, "position": 1}
